        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0353" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1915: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-31T13:00:00+03:25">August 31, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 31—12:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>275. My 265, August 21. Iranian Government has agreed to detention of the
                    suspects in British controlled area at Sultanabad. Prime Minister informs me he
                    obtained consent of Majlis to this procedure in secret session Saturday by
                    assuming full and personal responsibility. It is understood British Foreign
                    Office supported Tehran Legation in demanding detention at Sultanabad so that
                    Iranians had no alternative in end but to accept. This is last remaining point
                    at issue in this dispute and it is hoped that at least a temporary solution has
                    been reached. Whatever the merits of the case there is no doubt it has been very
                    harmful to British-Iranian relations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
